So the news by now are:
1. Server changed.
2. A lot of improvements in formatting of pages by several contributors. 
Especially in making the wiki less bound to particular languages. New icons 
in the left sidebar (it would be right sidebar for right-to-left languages)
3. Babel extension enabled
4. WikiArticleFeeds extension enabled
5. Update to MW 1.26 alpha, most extensions upgraded
6. Pdfexport extension enabled with mPDF (seems not to be working with East 
Asia fonts!)
7. Book extension disabled
8. "print as pdf" experimental link added to the left sidebar
9. LMW: Login page now displays all the languages for which we have front 
pages. http://mw.lojban.org/lmw/Special:UserLogin
10. SimpleMathJax enabled
11. Google Analytics upgraded to Universal Analytics, display features 
enabled (feel free to contact me to give access to GA to your Google 
accounts)
A known bug <https://github.com/paladox/Metrolook/issues/109> in Metrolook 
skin is that after clicking on an item in the table of contents the scroll 
position moves but one cannot scroll it back.

Also I think that Translate extension is somewhat inappropriate for using 
it everywhere, e.g. for the front page since for different languages we 
have different resources and sometimes it's pretty impossible to translate 
something optimized for speaker of a certain natlang.
However, we have some examples where it seems to be useful:
http://mw.lojban.org/papri/sepulka
http://mw.lojban.org/papri/lojbo%20sinxa


